      "writtenOn": "2023-05-18T16:55:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about adding a mandatory `label` part?\n\n```\n    \"BazelTest\": {\n      \"keys\": [\n        \"task_driver\",\n        \"label\",  // \u003c- New mandatory part.\n        \"config\",\n        \"host\"\n      ],\n      \"optional_keys\": [\n        \"cross\"\n      ]\n    },\n```\n\nThe task I\u0027m adding in this CL would then become `BazelTest-bazel_precompiled_test-android_codec_test-pixel_5-linux_x64`.\n\nThe rationale is that all existing task drivers already target a specific label, but the label is hardcoded into each task driver. Specifically:\n\n- `canvaskit_gold.go` tests `//modules/canvaskit:canvaskit_js_tests`.\n- `cpu_tests.go` tests `//tests/...`.\n- `toolchain_layering_check.go` builds `//experimental/bazel_test/client:client_lib`.\n\nSo under this proposal, we would make the labels explicit by pushing them to `gen_tasks_logic.go` and passing them to the task drivers via a new flag.\n\nAs an example, task `BazelTest-cpu_tests-cpu_only_debug_rbe-linux_x64` would become `BazelTest-cpu_tests-tests-cpu_only_debug_rbe-linux_x64`, where `tests` maps to `//tests/...`.",
      "parentUuid": "616d5f01_fe1bbf71",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "88861ebf9b6912a84337d19e12ac56d0df4c8653",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
